## 4. Critical Domain Rules & Business Invariants (NEVER VIOLATE)

### 4.1 The 12-Item Deterministic Scoring Matrix

The scoring logic MUST be implemented as pure functions in `backend/services/scoring/ItemScorers.js`. Total points: **100** on normal days; **82** on off-days.

| Item | Life Area | Input Type | Max | Exact Conversion Rule |
|---|---|---|:---:|---|
| **1** | Early Morning | Boolean | 8 | `val === true` $\rightarrow$ **8 pts**; `false` $\rightarrow$ **0 pts** |
| **2** | University Attendance | Enum (`yes`, `no`, `off_day`) | 10 | `'yes'` $\rightarrow$ **10 pts**; `'no'` $\rightarrow$ **0 pts**; `'off_day'` $\rightarrow$ **Excluded from denominator** |
| **3** | Class Participation | Fraction ($a / b$) | 8 | $\min\left(8, \max\left(0, \frac{a}{b} \times 8\right)\right)$; Guard: $b \ge 1, a \le b$; on `off_day` $\rightarrow$ **Excluded** |
| **4** | Personal Discipline | Boolean | 8 | `val === true` $\rightarrow$ **8 pts**; `false` $\rightarrow$ **0 pts** |
| **5** | Social Interaction | Integer ($\ge 0$) | 6 | $\ge 3 \rightarrow$ **6 pts**; $2 \rightarrow$ **4 pts**; $1 \rightarrow$ **2 pts**; $0 \rightarrow$ **0 pts** |
| **6** | Daily Learning | Text Note | 10 | `text.trim().length > 0` $\rightarrow$ **10 pts**; empty $\rightarrow$ **0 pts** (Max: 500 chars) |
| **7** | Physical Activity | Boolean + Minutes | 10 | `active === true` AND $\text{mins} \ge 15 \rightarrow$ **10 pts**; active with $< 15\text{m} \rightarrow$ **5 pts**; inactive $\rightarrow$ **0 pts** |
| **8** | Skill Development | Minutes ($\ge 0$) | 10 | $\ge 60\text{m} \rightarrow$ **10 pts**; $30\dots59\text{m} \rightarrow$ **6 pts**; $15\dots29\text{m} \rightarrow$ **3 pts**; $< 15\text{m} \rightarrow$ **0 pts** |
| **9** | Class Work Recap | Boolean | 10 | `val === true` $\rightarrow$ **10 pts**; `false` $\rightarrow$ **0 pts** |
| **10** | Social Media Control | 3-way Enum | 6 | `'controlled'` $\rightarrow$ **6 pts**; `'useful'` $\rightarrow$ **3 pts**; `'excessive'` $\rightarrow$ **0 pts** |
| **11** | Self-Reflection | Text Journal | 8 | `text.trim().length > 0` $\rightarrow$ **8 pts**; empty $\rightarrow$ **0 pts** (Max: 500 chars) |
| **12** | Sleeping on Time | Boolean | 6 | `val === true` $\rightarrow$ **6 pts**; `false` $\rightarrow$ **0 pts** |

#### Scoring Formula
$$\text{Daily Score (\%)} = \min\left(100.00, \max\left(0.00, \frac{\text{Points Achieved}}{\text{Max Available Points}} \times 100\right)\right)$$
- Normal Day: $\text{Max Available Points} = 100$
- Off Day (`item2 === 'off_day'`): Items 2 and 3 omitted $\rightarrow \text{Max Available Points} = 82$
- Round to **2 decimal places** (`+score.toFixed(2)`).

---

### 4.2 The 10 Life Stage Boundaries

In `backend/services/classification/LifeStageClassifier.js`, map `lifeScore` ($0.00 \dots 100.00$) to these exact ranges:

| Stage ID | Stage Title | Exact Score Range (%) |
|:---:|---|---|
| **1** | Critical / Highly Unbalanced | $0.00 \le \text{score} < 20.00$ |
| **2** | Struggling / Low Discipline | $20.00 \le \text{score} < 30.00$ |
| **3** | Inconsistent Routine | $30.00 \le \text{score} < 40.00$ |
| **4** | Emerging Awareness | $40.00 \le \text{score} < 50.00$ |
| **5** | Moderate Balance | $50.00 \le \text{score} < 60.00$ |
| **6** | Steady Progress | $60.00 \le \text{score} < 70.00$ |
| **7** | Disciplined Student | $70.00 \le \text{score} < 80.00$ |
| **8** | High Achiever | $80.00 \le \text{score} < 90.00$ |
| **9** | Exemplary Lifestyle | $90.00 \le \text{score} < 95.00$ |
| **10** | Exceptional Self-Development | $95.00 \le \text{score} \le 100.00$ |

*Rule:* Lower boundary is inclusive; upper boundary is exclusive (except Stage 10 where $100.00$ is inclusive).

---

### 4.3 Streak Lifecycle & Same-Day Edit Guardrails

The consecutive streak counter is stored in `cycles.currentStreak`.

1. **Brand-New Submission (`POST /api/v1/checklist`):**
   - Must increment streak: `currentStreak = currentStreak + 1`.
2. **Same-Day Edit (`PUT /api/v1/checklist/today`) & Grace Edit (`PUT /api/v1/checklist/yesterday`):**
   - **CRITICAL:** Recompute scores and update documents, but **DO NOT increment streak**.
3. **Midnight Missed-Day Cron (`0 0 * * *`):**
   - If yesterday was missed past grace window, insert dummy record with `totalScore: 0`, and **reset streak: `currentStreak = 0`**.

---

### 4.4 Timezone Offset Requirement

Clients transmit the `x-timezone-offset` header (minutes offset from UTC, e.g., `-360`).
- The backend MUST normalize transaction dates to the student's **local midnight**:
  ```javascript
  const getLocalMidnight = (date, timezoneOffsetMinutes) => {
    const utc = new Date(date);
    const local = new Date(utc.getTime() - timezoneOffsetMinutes * 60000);
    local.setUTCHours(0, 0, 0, 0);
    return local;
  };
  ```

---

## 5. Database & Mongoose Modeling Rules

1. **Explicit Collection Naming:** Use exact camelCase collection names:
   ```javascript
   { collection: 'dailyActivities' }
   { collection: 'dailyScores' }
   { collection: 'weeklySummaries' }
   { collection: 'monthlyResults' }
   { collection: 'pushSubscriptions' }
   ```
2. **Mandatory Unique Compound Indexes:**
   - `dailyActivities`: `{ userId: 1, date: 1 }` (Unique) $\rightarrow$ Blocks duplicate entries.
   - `dailyScores`: `{ userId: 1, date: 1 }` (Unique).
   - `weeklySummaries`: `{ userId: 1, cycleId: 1, weekNumber: 1 }` (Unique).
   - `monthlyResults`: `{ userId: 1, cycleId: 1 }` (Unique).
   - `pushSubscriptions`: `{ userId: 1, endpoint: 1 }` (Unique).
   - `cycles`: `{ userId: 1, status: 1 }` with `{ unique: true, partialFilterExpression: { status: 'active' } }` $\rightarrow$ Prevents multiple active cycles per user.
3. **ACID Transactions:** Any operation touching multiple collections (`DailyActivity` + `DailyScore` + `Cycle`) must use `mongoose.startSession()` and `session.startTransaction()`.

---

## 6. API Architecture & Error Handling Standards

### 6.1 Routing & Versioning
All endpoints MUST be prefixed with `/api/v1/...`.

### 6.2 Standard Response Envelopes
- **Success (200 / 201):**
  ```json
  { "success": true, "data": { ... }, "message": "..." }
  ```
- **Error (400 / 401 / 403 / 404 / 409 / 429 / 500):**
  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "error": {
      "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
      "message": "Human-readable description",
      "field": "item3_classParticipation_attended",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-20T21:45:00.000Z",
      "path": "/api/v1/checklist"
    }
  }
  ```

### 6.3 Standard Error Codes
Use the exact codes from `api-spec.md`:
- `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `INVALID_TIME_FORMAT`, `GRACE_WINDOW_EXPIRED`, `WEEK_NOT_UNLOCKED`, `CYCLE_NOT_COMPLETED`
- `UNAUTHORIZED`, `TOKEN_EXPIRED`, `INVALID_CREDENTIALS`
- `EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED`, `FORBIDDEN_RESOURCE`
- `NOT_FOUND`, `NO_ACTIVE_CYCLE`, `NO_ENTRY_TODAY`
- `EMAIL_ALREADY_EXISTS`, `ACTIVE_CYCLE_EXISTS`, `ALREADY_SUBMITTED_TODAY`

---

## 7. Frontend Architecture & UI Guidelines

1. **Next.js 14+ App Router**: Use route grouping:
   - `(auth)`: Login, registration, password recovery.
   - `(app)`: Dashboard, cycle setup, checklist, reports, settings (wrapped in `AuthGuard`).
2. **Axios Client Interceptors (`frontend/lib/axios.js`)**:
   - Automatically inject `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
   - Automatically inject `x-timezone-offset: new Date().getTimezoneOffset()`.
   - On 401 `TOKEN_EXPIRED`, clear storage and redirect to `/login`.
3. **Responsive Mobile-First UI**: Use Tailwind CSS. Students will primarily view and submit checklists on smartphones.
4. **Data Visualization**:
   - Use **Recharts** for 30-day score trend lines and weekly area breakdowns.
   - Use **Recharts RadarChart** for 30-day monthly lifestyle balance.

---

## 8. Phase-by-Phase Development Protocol

When executing the project, follow the phased roadmap defined in `prompt.md`:

```
Phase 0  ──► Project Scaffolding & Monorepo Setup
Phase 1  ──► MongoDB Connection, 7 Mongoose Schemas & Global Error Middleware
Phase 2  ──► Auth Subsystem (JWT, bcrypt, Verification, Cascaded Account Deletion)
Phase 3  ──► Cycle Lifecycle State Machine (Start, Active check, Day counter, Abandon)
Phase 4  ──► 12-Item Checklist Service, Pure Scoring Engine, Off-day & Streak logic
Phase 5  ──► Midnight Missed-Day Cron Job (0% Backfill & Streak Reset)
Phase 6  ──► Weekly & 30-Day Aggregation Pipelines (Life Stage & Insights)
Phase 7  ──► Web Push Service Worker (VAPID) & Milestone Emails
Phase 8  ──► Next.js App Router Shell, Tailwind Setup, Axios & AuthContext
Phase 9  ──► Dashboard UI, 12-Item Checklist Form & Daily Score Gauge
Phase 10 ──► Recharts Weekly Bar Breakdown & 30-Day Radar Life Stage Views
Phase 11 ──► End-to-End Testing, Security Audits (Rate Limit, XSS) & Dockerization
```

*Instruction for AI:* Never jump ahead to frontend phases before verifying that the corresponding backend API and domain tests pass.

---

## 9. Pre-Commit / Pre-Completion Verification Checklist

Before marking any phase or task as complete, verify every item:

- [ ] **Pure Scoring Engine:** Tested with normal day (max 100) and off-day (max 82). Results match Table 4.1 exactly.
- [ ] **Streak Non-Duplication:** Calling `PUT /api/v1/checklist/today` updates scores but leaves `currentStreak` unchanged.
- [ ] **Duplicate Guard:** Calling `POST /api/v1/checklist` twice for the same date returns `409 ALREADY_SUBMITTED_TODAY`.
- [ ] **Active Cycle Collisions:** Attempting to start a cycle while one is active returns `409 ACTIVE_CYCLE_EXISTS`.
- [ ] **Timezone Header:** Every date-sensitive endpoint normalizes dates using `x-timezone-offset`.
- [ ] **Cascaded Deletion:** Calling `DELETE /api/v1/users/me` removes records across all 7 collections without orphan data.
- [ ] **Error Envelope:** All error responses return `{ success: false, error: { code, message, field, timestamp, path } }`.
- [ ] **Data Isolation:** All database queries enforce `{ userId: req.user.userId }`.

